  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ABG: Realising the Faith Potential</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Realising the Faith Potential in Diocese of Marsabit is a developmental project seeking to address the urgent need to work through the prevailing challenges to good governance in this region that is highly dominated by nomadic pastoralist way of life.  Implementation will focus in areas covered by Marsabit diocese and will involve dealing with issues that form the basis for bad governance and transform them into opportunities with the aim of building a strong foundation for better governance. 

The project intends to facilitate various Church structures and other stakeholders to actively participate in building a good governance environment within their respective locality. The project will create opportunities for civic engagements and support citizens to articulate of their rights and collaborate for accountable and responsive governance. In order to make citizens to more confidently and effectively network, communicate, negotiate and collaborate with the state, the project plans among other things to engage grass root communities to come up with development plan and utilize the plan to lobby for development initiatives. In addition, it will also establish interfaith alliance and make use of coalitions of faith leaders in lobby and advocacy for better governance.

The Diocese of Marsabit is well placed due to its structural capacities (grassroots networks) and long term experience working with the pastoralist to play a major role alongside other partners in addressing the challenges.  Some of these issues include negative ethnicity, insecurity, weak government institutions, and outstanding boundary issues, among others.  The Diocese also has well established infrastructure for intervention but requires support in terms of resources to implement the proposed activities and consolidate the gains made. 
In order the deal with these issues the project will engage the national and local level governance structures including the ministries, provincial administration and security machineries. In addition the program will engage the management of all the devolved funds among them the Constituency Development Fund (CDF), Roads Fund, Bursary Fund and Local Authority Transfer Fund (LATF).

The project plans to work with Catholic Church leaders and Church structures. It will also work with Interfaith Alliance and make use of coalitions of faith leaders to lobby and advocate for better governance. On other the hand working existing community structures and other stakeholders shall be made a priority.</narrative>
  </description>
